<resources>
  <!--
    Debug builds install alongside the Play build (see applicationIdSuffix in
    build.gradle), so they need a launcher label that tells them apart. Two
    identical "Sabeel Kanban" icons side by side is worse than one.

    A build-type source set overrides src/main; declaring the same name with
    `resValue` in the debug buildType instead would be a duplicate-resource
    error, because src/main/res already defines app_name.

    THE DIFFERENCE MUST COME EARLY IN THE STRING. "Sabeel Kanban (dev)" was the
    obvious choice and was useless: the launcher truncates to about eleven
    characters, so both apps read "Sabeel Kanb..." under identical icons and
    nothing distinguished them. Leading with "Kanban dev" puts the difference
    where it survives truncation. Verified on the emulator, not assumed — the
    first version looked correct in the resource file and wrong on the screen.
  -->
  <string name="app_name">Kanban dev</string>
</resources>
